me":"Gerard Oosterhof"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T19:29:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(frontend): arrow functions only — adopt the six canonical oxlint rules (WR-1633) (#448)\n\nCommander ruling 2026-09-21: the codebase wants arrow functions only. A\n`function` declaration hoists and binds its own `this`; neither is wanted. The\ncanon only CLAIMED the convention in a comment and enforced nothing, so every\ntree the war room writes drifted. Six rules adopted from\n`war-room/templates/oxlintrc.json`, and the tree converted to satisfy them.\n\nRules (measured before → after, `oxlint --type-aware .` from `frontend/`,\noxlint 1.82, 310 lintable files):\n\n  func-style                   11 → 0   (2 files)\n  prefer-arrow-callback         4 → 0   (1 file)\n  arrow-body-style              6 → 0   (2 files)\n  no-use-before-define          0 → 0   (positive-controlled)\n  import/no-default-export      1 → 0   (covered by the override)\n  consistent-type-definitions   7 → 0   (4 files)\n\n`import/no-default-export` moves from `off` to `error` at the root, carrying\nthe canon override for the shapes that MUST default-export. BIO''s own\n`src/**/*.ts` → `error` override is dropped as redundant under the new root;\nits `*-reporter.ts` exemption stays. `*.config.mjs` is added to the override\nbecause `stryker.config.mjs` default-exports and the canon glob does not reach\na `.mjs` config.\n\n`MiddlewarePipelineVisualizer.vue` is reordered topologically: converting ten\ndeclarations to consts turns their forward references into TDZ reads, so each\nconst now sits above its first textual reference. Proved with the all-scope\nform of `no-use-before-define` (`variables: true`) as a one-off migration\ninstrument; the canon''s same-scope form is what ships.\n\nFour `vi.fn().mockImplementation(function () {...})` callbacks in\n`sound.spec.ts` stay declarations under a line-scoped disable: the service\nunder test calls `new AudioContext()`, and an arrow is not constructible —\nconverting them failed 7 tests before the residual was named.\n\nGates: oxlint, oxfmt, vue-tsc, lint:vue, knip, build, size, vitest\n(1418 unit + 150 integration), stryker (96.00 vs 90 floor) — all green.","tree":{"sha":"b44523018f38861aea0475ef767e7e80c342b01b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/git/trees/b44523018f38861aea0475ef767e7e80c342b01b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/git/commits/ff56b5a9ef29281fc61bde5f6d0e2e05dc6b77c8","verification":{"payload":"tree b44523018f38861aea0475ef767e7e80c342b01b\nparent ede1b5b7e519e593ab8d019daf1f3fba215d3d04\nauthor Gerard Oosterhof <gerard.oosterhof@gmail.com> 1790018983 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790018983 +0200\n\nchore(frontend): arrow functions only — adopt the six canonical oxlint rules (WR-1633) (#448)\n\nCommander ruling 2026-09-21: the codebase wants arrow functions only. A\n`function` declaration hoists and binds its own `this`; neither is wanted. The\ncanon only CLAIMED the convention in a comment and enforced nothing, so every\ntree the war room writes drifted. Six rules adopted from\n`war-room/templates/oxlintrc.json`, and the tree converted to satisfy them.\n\nRules (measured before → after, `oxlint --type-aware .` from `frontend/`,\noxlint 1.82, 310 lintable files):\n\n  func-style                   11 → 0   (2 files)\n  prefer-arrow-callback         4 → 0   (1 file)\n  arrow-body-style              6 → 0   (2 files)\n  no-use-before-define          0 → 0   (positive-controlled)\n  import/no-default-export      1 → 0   (covered by the override)\n  consistent-type-definitions   7 → 0   (4 files)\n\n`import/no-default-export` moves from `off` to `error` at the root, carrying\nthe canon override for the shapes that MUST default-export. BIO''s own\n`src/**/*.ts` → `error` override is dropped as redundant under the new root;\nits `*-reporter.ts` exemption stays. `*.config.mjs` is added to the override\nbecause `stryker.config.mjs` default-exports and the canon glob does not reach\na `.mjs` config.\n\n`MiddlewarePipelineVisualizer.vue` is reordered topologically: converting ten\ndeclarations to consts turns their forward references into TDZ reads, so each\nconst now sits above its first textual reference. Proved with the all-scope\nform of `no-use-before-define` (`variables: true`) as a one-off migration\ninstrument; the canon''s same-scope form is what ships.\n\nFour `vi.fn().mockImplementation(function () {...})` callbacks in\n`sound.spec.ts` stay declarations under a line-scoped disable: the service\nunder test calls `new AudioContext()`, and an arrow is not constructible —\nconverting them failed 7 tests before the residual was named.\n\nGates: oxlint, oxfmt, vue-tsc, lint:vue, knip, build, size, vitest\n(1418 unit + 150 integration), stryker (96.00 vs 90 floor) — all green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsYWnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbRMQACZ762fTgUP93Zjm25pcTrln\nn3NgKIYu9ZLBetmrkZDZfI65ieD1Vw4goFwr60ilmTjIc+KR1UaR+u9YwMBjlhU8\nJxxfVJkuzCJhpTMyjYR4KMvF5z/G2Sa7JarBAO9+V2ICZ8ojlyFka11KGGk5HJ2I\nWb9RXf26Hw0Uq2cUSd/8tuktC6jkDtwilUIz+zdPcrXgv4WkXD6yA/vJeKKXF1Cu\nzmNhOnnaqzIQSbh9RC57O1uN29VC0I6IYTuGQRT91DtGfURINa7dZ5RsH9E3W2Mn\n9wrC+AjWkNiBDmHsXZxICyjeO7KI/JbFHiOxFJxm9pgfffqD6UhX0aSrZuF8xjhj\n7lHPQUGOMFEvT/MiozWhgip3SL6Tsn+9EvPc4HUT9+B+/3x3r0I4Vg2ZNN5Goaxs\n0EnFjUeJHj7J8jHrdUU7auF8R/HoCVCZ0Gl2iykGsMpOg7PUPSP3/By6Xfoy8sRn\nb7T8gHVsSUV6Z2mRJZ3z24pHNdSs7WzLXUmC5XeIHtzAYRt/wPLRyxJQjfT/HMj5\n1TvYo9Jyg+L0V+d/WWleXez9bi9O/KZFJF3t0aFsMsjjHDYsHRCKnETv7Zu0YgRW\n5SHDD4VUn7yA+UG2Krb1e1yhpoPb1wotB7PyyQTkuonXczoTxvN2BtmKKzuz77LF\nHb6CCRQ3zBMfy8Hclgd2\n=6V75\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T19:29:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commit/ff56b5a9ef29281fc61bde5f6d0e2e05dc6b77c8","node_id":"C_kwDORGtmsNoAKGZmNTZiNWE5ZWYyOTI4MWZjNjFiZGU1ZjZkMGUyZTA1ZGM2Yjc3Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commit/ede1b5b7e519e593ab8d019daf1f3fba215d3d04","sha":"ede1b5b7e519e593ab8d019daf1f3fba215d3d04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commits/ede1b5b7e519e593ab8d019daf1f3fba215d3d04"}],"sha":"ff56b5a9ef29281fc61bde5f6d0e2e05dc6b77c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commits/ff56b5a9ef29281fc61bde5f6d0e2e05dc6b77c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24678549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Goosterhof","id":24678549,"login":"Goosterhof","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0Njc4NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commits/ede1b5b7e519e593ab8d019daf1f3fba215d3d04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:31:51Z","email":"gerard.oosterhof@gmail.com","name":"Gerard Oosterhof"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:31:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): adopt the Armory group — fs-{adapter-store,dialog,form,router} + ui-inputs 0.13 (#447)\n\nFive @script-development minor bumps Dependabot could not land blind (#439, #424),\nwith the two consumer-side migrations they require.\n\nui-inputs 0.13 promotes the select/combobox menu anchor to the top layer in place\n(popover=\"manual\", KD-1136) and calls showPopover() unconditionally — the Popover API\nis Baseline 2024, so the package carries no capability branch. happy-dom 20 implements\nnone of it, which took down 7 integration cases across AddSetPage and PartsUnsortedPage:\nthe visible `Cannot read properties of null (reading ''$'')` was teardown after the\nwatcher threw, not a render-shape change. Shimmed in the integration setup alongside\nthe existing HTMLDialogElement and HTMLMediaElement polyfills, mirroring the package''s\nown tests/popover-shim.ts. The real 0.13 components run; nothing is stubbed.\n\nfs-router 0.3 returns vue-router''s navigation promise from install() (0.2 was\n`() => void router.push(...)`), so all three app entry points floated a promise —\n`typescript(no-floating-promises)` failed the lint gate on each. Voided at the call\nsite, which is the pre-bump behaviour rather than a new swallow. WR-1455.\n\nfs-dialog''s closeOnBackdropClick defaults to true, fs-form''s scrollToError ships\nfalse, and no BIO code subscribes to an adapter-store broadcast — those three are\ninert here. Peer graph clean (npm ls: no invalid). One transitive moved:\nvue-component-type-helpers 3.3.8 -> 3.3.11.\n\nGates: lint 0 errors (17 pre-existing warnings), lint:vue pass, knip pass,\nformat:check 338 files, type-check 0, coverage 112 files / 1418 tests / 100%,\nmutation 96.00% (9 files, 250 mutants, per-file floor held), integration 20 files /\n150 tests, build 3 apps, size within limits.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dbcc7ad78c20d68cb82381597970079218a3cebc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/git/trees/dbcc7ad78c20d68cb82381597970079218a3cebc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/git/commits/ede1b5b7e519e593ab8d019daf1f3fba215d3d04","verification":{"payload":"tree dbcc7ad78c20d68cb82381597970079218a3cebc\nparent 2976be7b2ba67a8f9c862d38ebcf8c1359deee23\nauthor Gerard Oosterhof <gerard.oosterhof@gmail.com> 1790001111 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790001111 +0000\n\nchore(deps): adopt the Armory group — fs-{adapter-store,dialog,form,router} + ui-inputs 0.13 (#447)\n\nFive @script-development minor bumps Dependabot could not land blind (#439, #424),\nwith the two consumer-side migrations they require.\n\nui-inputs 0.13 promotes the select/combobox menu anchor to the top layer in place\n(popover=\"manual\", KD-1136) and calls showPopover() unconditionally — the Popover API\nis Baseline 2024, so the package carries no capability branch. happy-dom 20 implements\nnone of it, which took down 7 integration cases across AddSetPage and PartsUnsortedPage:\nthe visible `Cannot read properties of null (reading ''$'')` was teardown after the\nwatcher threw, not a render-shape change. Shimmed in the integration setup alongside\nthe existing HTMLDialogElement and HTMLMediaElement polyfills, mirroring the package''s\nown tests/popover-shim.ts. The real 0.13 components run; nothing is stubbed.\n\nfs-router 0.3 returns vue-router''s navigation promise from install() (0.2 was\n`() => void router.push(...)`), so all three app entry points floated a promise —\n`typescript(no-floating-promises)` failed the lint gate on each. Voided at the call\nsite, which is the pre-bump behaviour rather than a new swallow. WR-1455.\n\nfs-dialog''s closeOnBackdropClick defaults to true, fs-form''s scrollToError ships\nfalse, and no BIO code subscribes to an adapter-store broadcast — those three are\ninert here. Peer graph clean (npm ls: no invalid). One transitive moved:\nvue-component-type-helpers 3.3.8 -> 3.3.11.\n\nGates: lint 0 errors (17 pre-existing warnings), lint:vue pass, knip pass,\nformat:check 338 files, type-check 0, coverage 112 files / 1418 tests / 100%,\nmutation 96.00% (9 files, 250 mutants, per-file floor held), integration 20 files /\n150 tests, build 3 apps, size within limits.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsT/XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIjsQAEVMpBUhT9QkxOhtSSzK2kIM\nM8UGfAYBU2bCS2txOjMjc0YsMi/xgLtZ45bnVMyJ3/FCwuu3Ffai3RYDUOnaeYkA\nJt9Dg8DWgIE6OKxxAXmvqZJ0Adft1/QDBv7tSd+ljRX+1OUA7wVsVFiFiVzTJSNA\n6REQMcYQN3kZ8/AYEH2UlJABGyTeLeBj0tz+VI1Z1PaDvVagX8I4YQJ7cbqt3O6b\nM4nSBSg7UZ493FBpmF6pF332zWXhCBCVpE+3D2pHPKCNt3PI8fW0v4OGHPkspE2X\n613bVToBrZMmoKCGZQ7j0L/hnM0bb9B1YWfEg9Tbn/figEhyEiwCbe0Tzz8Dmd9Z\n4J4xDBW7+k+bGHrbGIqlxKpEwE89xIS6vfwGh5e7pkULlL02k8gjVu6IJJ4soh2W\nq/EmcXIHyApsXucsJmajV7r/KqIuK5t6blY87BaNRleIaZy42GlzCK2oCveeA1/x\nfZpKUWlpwleGlba2TOyVWYdtk9Yf3W4n38ifj6+w9708Vq87RiUu3MouXdkbKl3j\nOYzgUYZCgPT6/P0AjEnE/saPhdkyNntPkQW5CE+q2UmJy+CvZ2SJFLaQpI8UsUJU\nHSwBP0aVaKTe6LJQFGNpL8LergD9nnK/Jqshjw8gXGyIbgoj+RA172K+MGUVTzU9\nTbGxojvtky0Pm7+ZQuk2\n=lUcr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T14:31:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commit/ede1b5b7e519e593ab8d019daf1f3fba215d3d04","node_id":"C_kwDORGtmsNoAKGVkZTFiNWI3ZTUxOWU1OTNhYjhkMDE5ZGFmMWYzZmJhMjE1ZDNkMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commit/2976be7b2ba67a8f9c862d38ebcf8c1359deee23","sha":"2976be7b2ba67a8f9c862d38ebcf8c1359deee23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commits/2976be7b2ba67a8f9c862d38ebcf8c1359deee23"}],"sha":"ede1b5b7e519e593ab8d019daf1f3fba215d3d04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commits/ede1b5b7e519e593ab8d019daf1f3fba215d3d04"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24678549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Goosterhof","id":24678549,"login":"Goosterhof","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0Njc4NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commits/2976be7b2ba67a8f9c862d38ebcf8c1359deee23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:28:17Z","email":"gerard.oosterhof@gmail.com","name":"Gerard Oosterhof"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T14:28:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps-dev): bump the backend dev-tooling group with rector 2.6.7 applied (supersedes #434, #417) (#445)\n\n* fix(hooks): hand CaptainHook the repo-root .git entry, not the resolved common dir\n\nCaptainHook derives the repository root as dirname(--git-directory) and\nverifies it with is_dir(root/.git) || is_file(root/.git). Passing the\nabsolute common dir made the root `.git/modules/territories` in a\nsubmodule checkout and refused every backend commit with \"Invalid git\nrepository\". `$repo_root/.git` is what it wants: a directory in a\nstandalone clone, a gitdir pointer file in a worktree or submodule —\nboth accepted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump the backend dev-tooling group with rector 2.6.7 applied\n\nSupersedes dependabot #434 (deptrac 4.7.2, larastan 3.12.x, rector 2.6.7)\nand #417 (driftingly/rector-laravel 2.6.2). Both went red on `rector:test`\nbecause rector 2.6.7 ships DirnameDirConcatStringToDirectStringPathRector\nand rector-laravel 2.6.2 ships AddGenericBuilderToScopesRector; a bare\nlockfile bump can never pass its own lint gate. This lands the bump with\n`composer rector` applied: two dirname(__DIR__) rewrites in the test\nhelpers and a Builder<static> generic on InviteCode::active().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(arch): anchor the relative-path strip at tests/, where getTestFiles() builds its paths\n\nFour assertion messages stripped `__DIR__ . ''/../''` off paths that\ngetTestFiles() had built from Pest.php''s own __DIR__, so the strip no\nlonger matched after the rector rewrite and a failure would have printed\nthe absolute path. relativeTestPath() lives beside getTestFiles() and\nrealpath()s both sides (WR-1622).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c6321e738b2f029a759282c268ac981a9194b31e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/git/trees/c6321e738b2f029a759282c268ac981a9194b31e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/git/commits/2976be7b2ba67a8f9c862d38ebcf8c1359deee23","verification":{"payload":"tree c6321e738b2f029a759282c268ac981a9194b31e\nparent c6dbfe9f93db54ec78334561ef772ddcf7815cf7\nauthor Gerard Oosterhof <gerard.oosterhof@gmail.com> 1790000897 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790000897 +0000\n\nchore(deps-dev): bump the backend dev-tooling group with rector 2.6.7 applied (supersedes #434, #417) (#445)\n\n* fix(hooks): hand CaptainHook the repo-root .git entry, not the resolved common dir\n\nCaptainHook derives the repository root as dirname(--git-directory) and\nverifies it with is_dir(root/.git) || is_file(root/.git). Passing the\nabsolute common dir made the root `.git/modules/territories` in a\nsubmodule checkout and refused every backend commit with \"Invalid git\nrepository\". `$repo_root/.git` is what it wants: a directory in a\nstandalone clone, a gitdir pointer file in a worktree or submodule —\nboth accepted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump the backend dev-tooling group with rector 2.6.7 applied\n\nSupersedes dependabot #434 (deptrac 4.7.2, larastan 3.12.x, rector 2.6.7)\nand #417 (driftingly/rector-laravel 2.6.2). Both went red on `rector:test`\nbecause rector 2.6.7 ships DirnameDirConcatStringToDirectStringPathRector\nand rector-laravel 2.6.2 ships AddGenericBuilderToScopesRector; a bare\nlockfile bump can never pass its own lint gate. This lands the bump with\n`composer rector` applied: two dirname(__DIR__) rewrites in the test\nhelpers and a Builder<static> generic on InviteCode::active().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(arch): anchor the relative-path strip at tests/, where getTestFiles() builds its paths\n\nFour assertion messages stripped `__DIR__ . ''/../''` off paths that\ngetTestFiles() had built from Pest.php''s own __DIR__, so the strip no\nlonger matched after the rector rewrite and a failure would have printed\nthe absolute path. relativeTestPath() lives beside getTestFiles() and\nrealpath()s both sides (WR-1622).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsT8BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW/8QACCcBt7RR0UIwY6K9FsJY6nr\njuhZtMKeO97u5FEmnDRsT9K0ITo8PhAr3lHcNGkA+KJvH2/ldbKBS1YMwcVhb9lL\nW9eIFDUc+jXd5tm5pEQ8YQslvkQpzSN1A37sCzkcvhEFf76BcpTlo3Afqkd7bOTr\nvmw+wnwSX8bLtBsOcjOI8n1AJ3kKuJOOJYA7L7rgk4L6L+W/HFXJqR53U869mjQn\npNl+Ke04XAXrTTI6CNH2xOKjGYkFzu1vWHG0RylszrMurLK+IH+nzzAtbm3y9KRV\nIpbXtLf/Hw/lkRdfYe9w1B2BOc3/uiftx+NHZt6UB+MGmFTOiwjjVmyT54QJZWln\nqtT0AFyaxK36eGX9jpqtYzk9p1L4NVtsWOOvVzzHOUWGYEkdjJtURziis/9xsOSq\nvdqXeSU4IzfvRWta4YuOx04ADCDyrGCxGzK