nventory-orchestrator/commits/66d4601c82e5fde3ffba1d8a5f530d6a0db8518f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24678549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Goosterhof","id":24678549,"login":"Goosterhof","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0Njc4NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goosterhof","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commits/d960538a99255a711860f87c96474c6131108537/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T09:49:54Z","email":"gerard.oosterhof@gmail.com","name":"Gerard Oosterhof"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T09:49:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(backend): adopt phpstan-warroom-rules ^0.8 + close the two gaps it surfaced (WR-0533, queue #140) (#380)\n\n* chore(backend): adopt phpstan-warroom-rules ^0.8 (WR-0533)\n\nBumps the pin from ^0.7 to ^0.8. The caret excludes the minor on 0.x, so\nat ^0.7 the three rules added in v0.8.0 were not in the installed tree —\nenrolled but inert. Solo update; the lock moves one package only.\n\nRules activated: EnforceActionResultDtoRule,\nForbidInlineArrayJsonResponseInControllersRule,\nForbidRawExceptionMessageInResponseRule.\n\nGate result: 7 fires. Three are suppressed inline with a reason —\none ResourceData-collection payload the rule''s isArray() gate cannot\ndistinguish from a bare array, and two single-key acks (the noise class\nthe rule''s own docblock tells consumers to separate out). Four are left\nUNSUPPRESSED as real gaps parked for their own dispatches: the feedback\nAction''s untyped vendor-body return plus its controller pass-through,\nand the two SetController sync-status payloads that need a\nComputedResourceData. composer phpstan therefore stays honestly red on\nthose four until the follow-ups land.\n\nForbidRawExceptionMessageInResponseRule fires zero, and it is a\n\"none findable\" zero, not a clean bill of health: laravel/mcp is not\ninstalled and no Laravel\\Mcp surface exists, so the always-armed default\nsink has no call sites. rawExceptionMessageSinks is deliberately left\nunarmed. The rule was teeth-proved live by temporarily arming a throwaway\nsink and injecting $e->getMessage() at a live catch site; it fired, and\nthe probe was reverted byte-for-byte (md5-verified).\n\nGreen: pint:test, rector:test, test:arch (115), deptrac (0 violations),\ntest (719).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rixcg4btkfkU9bATLz4EMP\n\n* fix(backend): close the two ADR-0009/0020 gaps the pwr 0.8 bump surfaced\n\nBoth defects were invisible while this repo sat on phpstan-warroom-rules\n^0.7 — caret excludes the minor on 0.x, so the v0.8.0 rules were never in\nthe installed tree. Adopting ^0.8 (497cb01) surfaced them and parked them\nas WR-0862 and WR-0863; this closes both, taking `composer phpstan` from\n4 errors to 0.\n\nItem A (WR-0862) — SubmitFeedbackAction returned a third-party body verbatim\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\nexecute() returned array<string, mixed> straight out of KendoReports::submit()\n— the raw decoded body of the Kendo API''s 201, a shape another team owns —\nand FeedbackController put it on the wire unchanged.\n\nNow returns SubmitFeedbackResultData, pinning the one field this app owns a\nmeaning for: the created report''s id. The controller emits it through\nSubmitFeedbackResourceData.\n\nThe row flagged \"which fields to pin\" as a product call. Measured instead:\nthe endpoint''s only consumer (FeedbackModal.vue:79) awaits the POST and\ndiscards the body — toast, reset, close. It reads no field, declares no\nresponse type, and passes no generic to postRequest. Nothing else in the\nfrontend or e2e references the endpoint. So the 201 narrows from the echoed\nKendo payload to {\"id\": <int|null>} with no consumer affected.\n\nreportId is nullable because the package''s swallow mode (report-tool.swallow,\ndisabled here) yields no body; that branch was already covered by a test.\n\nItem B (WR-0863) — sync-status built domain payloads inline\n-----------------------------------------------------------\nrespondForSyncStatus() constructed two three-field domain payloads inline\n(502 Failed, 202 Pending/InProgress). Now two ComputedResourceData classes,\nSetPartsSyncFailedResourceData and SetPartsSyncPendingResourceData.\n\nTwo classes rather than one with nullable fields, because the branches carry\ndifferent keys (`reason` vs `message`) — a single class would emit a null key\nneither response currently carries. The wire is therefore byte-identical, and\nevery pre-existing SetController test passed untouched, which is the evidence.\n\nWR-0863 also claimed ComputedResourceData has no toResponseWithStatus() and\nthat only ResourceData does. That is false at HEAD — ComputedResourceData.php:65\nhas it. Both branches use it directly; no base-class change was needed. The row\nhas been corrected.\n\nNotes\n-----\nSubmitFeedbackResultData carries no factory method: DtoArchitectureTest\nrequires Result DTOs expose only __construct, so the Kendo-body mapping lives\nin the Action, which is already the vendor seam. The arch test was respected,\nnot relaxed.\n\nAdded a numeric-string-id test. The (int) cast otherwise left a live\nRemoveIntegerCast mutant — the fakes all return an int, so nothing killed it.\nBackend mutation: 138 -> 136 untested, 80.15% -> 80.35%.\n\nVerified with the gates CI itself runs (.github/workflows/backend-ci.yml):\n\n  lint:test              pass\n  phpstan                No errors  (was 4)\n  phpstan:types          No errors\n  deptrac                pass\n  test:arch              115 passed\n  test                   720 passed (3172 assertions)\n  test:coverage          100.0%\n  test:feature-coverage  100.0%\n  mutation               80.35% (min 76)\n\nCommitted from a standalone clone with hooks fully engaged, because the\nCaptainHook pre-commit dispatch crashes in a war-room submodule checkout\n(WR-0864). No --no-verify was used. The hook was teeth-proved in this clone\nfirst: a planted inline-array JsonResponse was rejected by `composer phpstan`\nbefore this commit was made.\n\nCloses WR-0862. Closes WR-0863.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HJ7AobcmickSXLybYoAcra\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"656f21d6e28f0a48efe381d997f6c1bc5e3f402e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/git/trees/656f21d6e28f0a48efe381d997f6c1bc5e3f402e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/git/commits/d960538a99255a711860f87c96474c6131108537","verification":{"payload":"tree 656f21d6e28f0a48efe381d997f6c1bc5e3f402e\nparent b2eaf15fbf98fa854c7b3ddca060d08cefd75e85\nauthor Gerard Oosterhof <gerard.oosterhof@gmail.com> 1787824194 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787824194 +0200\n\nchore(backend): adopt phpstan-warroom-rules ^0.8 + close the two gaps it surfaced (WR-0533, queue #140) (#380)\n\n* chore(backend): adopt phpstan-warroom-rules ^0.8 (WR-0533)\n\nBumps the pin from ^0.7 to ^0.8. The caret excludes the minor on 0.x, so\nat ^0.7 the three rules added in v0.8.0 were not in the installed tree —\nenrolled but inert. Solo update; the lock moves one package only.\n\nRules activated: EnforceActionResultDtoRule,\nForbidInlineArrayJsonResponseInControllersRule,\nForbidRawExceptionMessageInResponseRule.\n\nGate result: 7 fires. Three are suppressed inline with a reason —\none ResourceData-collection payload the rule''s isArray() gate cannot\ndistinguish from a bare array, and two single-key acks (the noise class\nthe rule''s own docblock tells consumers to separate out). Four are left\nUNSUPPRESSED as real gaps parked for their own dispatches: the feedback\nAction''s untyped vendor-body return plus its controller pass-through,\nand the two SetController sync-status payloads that need a\nComputedResourceData. composer phpstan therefore stays honestly red on\nthose four until the follow-ups land.\n\nForbidRawExceptionMessageInResponseRule fires zero, and it is a\n\"none findable\" zero, not a clean bill of health: laravel/mcp is not\ninstalled and no Laravel\\Mcp surface exists, so the always-armed default\nsink has no call sites. rawExceptionMessageSinks is deliberately left\nunarmed. The rule was teeth-proved live by temporarily arming a throwaway\nsink and injecting $e->getMessage() at a live catch site; it fired, and\nthe probe was reverted byte-for-byte (md5-verified).\n\nGreen: pint:test, rector:test, test:arch (115), deptrac (0 violations),\ntest (719).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rixcg4btkfkU9bATLz4EMP\n\n* fix(backend): close the two ADR-0009/0020 gaps the pwr 0.8 bump surfaced\n\nBoth defects were invisible while this repo sat on phpstan-warroom-rules\n^0.7 — caret excludes the minor on 0.x, so the v0.8.0 rules were never in\nthe installed tree. Adopting ^0.8 (497cb01) surfaced them and parked them\nas WR-0862 and WR-0863; this closes both, taking `composer phpstan` from\n4 errors to 0.\n\nItem A (WR-0862) — SubmitFeedbackAction returned a third-party body verbatim\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\nexecute() returned array<string, mixed> straight out of KendoReports::submit()\n— the raw decoded body of the Kendo API''s 201, a shape another team owns —\nand FeedbackController put it on the wire unchanged.\n\nNow returns SubmitFeedbackResultData, pinning the one field this app owns a\nmeaning for: the created report''s id. The controller emits it through\nSubmitFeedbackResourceData.\n\nThe row flagged \"which fields to pin\" as a product call. Measured instead:\nthe endpoint''s only consumer (FeedbackModal.vue:79) awaits the POST and\ndiscards the body — toast, reset, close. It reads no field, declares no\nresponse type, and passes no generic to postRequest. Nothing else in the\nfrontend or e2e references the endpoint. So the 201 narrows from the echoed\nKendo payload to {\"id\": <int|null>} with no consumer affected.\n\nreportId is nullable because the package''s swallow mode (report-tool.swallow,\ndisabled here) yields no body; that branch was already covered by a test.\n\nItem B (WR-0863) — sync-status built domain payloads inline\n-----------------------------------------------------------\nrespondForSyncStatus() constructed two three-field domain payloads inline\n(502 Failed, 202 Pending/InProgress). Now two ComputedResourceData classes,\nSetPartsSyncFailedResourceData and SetPartsSyncPendingResourceData.\n\nTwo classes rather than one with nullable fields, because the branches carry\ndifferent keys (`reason` vs `message`) — a single class would emit a null key\nneither response currently carries. The wire is therefore byte-identical, and\nevery pre-existing SetController test passed untouched, which is the evidence.\n\nWR-0863 also claimed ComputedResourceData has no toResponseWithStatus() and\nthat only ResourceData does. That is false at HEAD — ComputedResourceData.php:65\nhas it. Both branches use it directly; no base-class change was needed. The row\nhas been corrected.\n\nNotes\n-----\nSubmitFeedbackResultData carries no factory method: DtoArchitectureTest\nrequires Result DTOs expose only __construct, so the Kendo-body mapping lives\nin the Action, which is already the vendor seam. The arch test was respected,\nnot relaxed.\n\nAdded a numeric-string-id test. The (int) cast otherwise left a live\nRemoveIntegerCast mutant — the fakes all return an int, so nothing killed it.\nBackend mutation: 138 -> 136 untested, 80.15% -> 80.35%.\n\nVerified with the gates CI itself runs (.github/workflows/backend-ci.yml):\n\n  lint:test              pass\n  phpstan                No errors  (was 4)\n  phpstan:types          No errors\n  deptrac                pass\n  test:arch              115 passed\n  test                   720 passed (3172 assertions)\n  test:coverage          100.0%\n  test:feature-coverage  100.0%\n  mutation               80.35% (min 76)\n\nCommitted from a standalone clone with hooks fully engaged, because the\nCaptainHook pre-commit dispatch crashes in a war-room submodule checkout\n(WR-0864). No --no-verify was used. The hook was teeth-proved in this clone\nfirst: a planted inline-array JsonResponse was rejected by `composer phpstan`\nbefore this commit was made.\n\nCloses WR-0862. Closes WR-0863.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HJ7AobcmickSXLybYoAcra\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkAhCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXyUQAIta1cusPM65w+3ZgIFH3uRw\n2UQMW2cfPCzDoqFuQ92cvME7glKW3z8AjS/TZVU3gC/Atx37bGmhVGNTro0vncE9\n3kqd+i4YAd0S2H7vAfxWuMsKh0hAXXHc1ApLac263XrUyWaJ4HeG8GKxzGp1qMYE\noWbX0/K69Sto29LlA79wrB1/2apCXsXdOhBOF5IcZGzG1qYnYIC8Hq+xs88Z/euD\nnf689RydZX1WF1sWuHAsdv4X1lsoKw+OWYdK9uCg9jvgrGBEsWysnKx0DUKoTQY4\n8TfwrGkdOWquSLykxkIlr56Er32RDrLrvo0nGaoLLdsqLHiTmmPnzh2bHjlLoEDz\nLAAII+koozR1I+89o792gr8XJU9WthlPF0z96w3/Qqea9x+AzoypNHzNFNKAGiWS\nn5ARC7B0844EAjoac6uDTpPQe4QlGa5O9gBIPkDnpauvZY0EJbYZHGAijMfH56M3\nGeGJ0NGlOcPWhsWJEyhnLl+RP+v8i6f7q565QyPQDHfbXpE9gEP4XkOvzS/pPDBv\nShTvKcrqb9aU3dOhDoSbvDNdPEsM/wKIVIudG5e41CNGHQqE4iaXcaXNaJMX6vcY\nuXJr0gw8RZhWBhlAz9ijIefZmXbCNHQM+J5RbAa4qB77t3lyutc5qgFpIJxTcmRs\nwRgHD7mxVv6H/+ZdJ8UZ\n=XlT+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T09:49:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commit/d960538a99255a711860f87c96474c6131108537","node_id":"C_kwDORGtmsNoAKGQ5NjA1MzhhOTkyNTVhNzExODYwZjg3Yzk2NDc0YzYxMzExMDg1Mzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commit/b2eaf15fbf98fa854c7b3ddca060d08cefd75e85","sha":"b2eaf15fbf98fa854c7b3ddca060d08cefd75e85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Goosterhof/brick-inventory-orchestrator/commits/b2eaf15fbf98fa854c7b3ddca060d08cefd75e85"}],"sha":"d960538a99255a711860f87c964