rl":"https://api.github.com/repos/chris-arsenault/the-canonry/commits/439e9029d4c1126448f0ebfede320acc45aa70ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-03T19:28:34Z","email":"carsena2@gmail.com","name":"Chris Arsenault"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-03T19:28:34Z","email":"carsena2@gmail.com","name":"Chris Arsenault"},"message":"feat(lint): add no-undefined-css-class rule — detect className strings without CSS definitions\n\nCatches the class of bug where className=\"some-class\" is used in JSX but\nno CSS file defines .some-class. This was invisible to tsc and caused the\nMFE pane overlap regression (canonry-remote-pane-hidden never defined).\n\nThe rule:\n- Parses side-effect CSS imports (import \"./Foo.css\") for class definitions\n- Scans co-located and sibling CSS files in the component directory\n- Scans configurable global style directories (shared-components/styles)\n- Checks string literals, template literal static segments, and ternary branches\n- Skips CSS module references (styles.foo) — already type-checked\n- Caches parsed CSS files for performance\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be423f1aaf6295a7b3905b71d59a905b7ef2111c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chris-arsenault/the-canonry/git/trees/be423f1aaf6295a7b3905b71d59a905b7ef2111c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chris-arsenault/the-canonry/git/commits/439e9029d4c1126448f0ebfede320acc45aa70ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5192503?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris-arsenault/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris-arsenault/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris-arsenault/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chris-arsenault/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ch