kube workspace directory\n- Show what is NOT deleted (host workspace, Docker images)\n- Provide commands to manually clean up remaining items\n- Remind user to stop minikube mount process\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01V73h5bf6iomUsp2EwZzQ4A","tree":{"sha":"f19a29a555d56434f7424612c87bdec67e84a12e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tedescomicchidev/MultiClaudeMCPTest/git/trees/f19a29a555d56434f7424612c87bdec67e84a12e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tedescomicchidev/MultiClaudeMCPTest/git/commits/d8000aee523bc6c2d6c9a8e555cdb3c6e9e4def1","verification":{"payload":"tree f19a29a555d56434f7424612c87bdec67e84a12e\nparent 4121fba34b45a01c5d4ddc44002151e963ef556f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1770158040 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1770158040 +0000\n\nImprove deploy.sh and cleanup.sh scripts\n\ndeploy.sh improvements:\n- Show HOST_WORKSPACE and MINIKUBE_WORKSPACE at startup\n- Use kubectl create configmap with --dry-run for idempotent updates\n- Add prominent box highlighting the minikube mount requirement\n- Show the exact minikube mount command to run\n- Add verification commands for workspace config\n- Better organized output sections\n\ncleanup.sh improvements:\n- Delete resources explicitly (deployments, services, configmaps, secrets, PVCs)\n- Clean up workspace-config ConfigMap\n- Clean up Minikube workspace directory\n- Show what is NOT deleted (host workspace, Docker images)\n- Provide commands to manually clean up remaining items\n- Remind user to stop minikube mount process\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01V73h5bf6iomUsp2EwZzQ4A\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK2JV7eh\nFKm/p4VkdcerMX6L3nX8tVgTTLbeGyZaYEaXrROkbXSPrgjVbzNHhpOtOcjlkX0cU5ek2DixvKav\nxQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-03T22:34:09Z"}},"committer